    "number": 189,
    "title": "Show shared agent status on the Tidbyt",
    "body": "## Problem\n\n#19 asks the Tidbyt to show shared agent status. The #16 controller could push a frame, but nothing turned agent-state snapshots into frames, and it had no way to take its installation out of rotation.\n\n## Result\n\n- **Status view and frame** (`status.ts`, `font.ts`): a pure function of one agent-state snapshot. It shows up to four rows. `ASK` means attention, `RUN` means active, and `DONE` means an unacknowledged turn-ended notice. Rows are ordered by state, then newest evidence, and a fourth `+N MORE` row covers overflow. Child and idle sessions are left out. Labels use the user label, then the project ID, then a neutral hashed ID (`C-3F9A`). Uncertain freshness dims the row and uses a `?` marker. An unreadable feed or a stopped collector marks every row that way, or shows `FEED ?`.\n- **Publisher** (`publisher.ts`): reads the owner's `snapshot()` and optional `subscribe()` and writes only through the controller queue. It pushes on change at most every 15 s, coalescing to the latest state. It refreshes an unchanged frame after 10 minutes and polls every 30 s. It removes the installation once when a healthy feed shows nothing. It never replays a failed write, never removes on an unavailable feed, never reduces events and never acknowledges notices.\n- **Controller removal**: `tidbyt.remove` (profile `tidbyt-display` 1.1.0) goes through the same admission, FIFO, generation check, holds and receipts as a push. The connection sends `DELETE /v0/devices/{device}/installations/{installation}`, which #16 qualified.\n- The decisions are recorded in `controllers/tidbyt/README.md#agent-status-decisions`. The OpenSpec change `gh-19-tidbyt-agent-status` is synced (new `tidbyt-agent-status` spec, plus one requirement added to `tidbyt-cloud-controller`) and archived.\n\nThe user settled the layout (four rows), cadence (on change, 15 s minimum, 10 minute refresh) and rotation (background installation, removed when idle) on 2026-09-23 before implementation.\n\n## Acceptance evidence\n\n- Decisions recorded in the Tidbyt README: yes.\n- Fake-feed and fake-transport tests: 20 new cases in `status.test.mjs` and `publisher.test.mjs`, which use a real in-memory agent-state owner, fake timers and a fake connection. They cover multiple sessions, a stale, unavailable or slow feed, failed and uncertain pushes, coalescing, refresh and idle removal. Removal cases were added to the connection and controller tests. Targeted mutations of the publisher (minimum interval, refresh, repeated removal, last good snapshot, uncertain handling, subscription, deferral) each fail at least one test.\n- Local checks at `23a5069` on Node 24.20.0 and Python 3.14.4 with pinned Pillow: `npm run build`, `typecheck`, `test:contracts`, `test:contracts:python`, `test:package`, `test:tidbyt` (57 pass), `test:tidbyt:python`, `test:agent-state`, `test:agent-state:python`, `check:workflow` and `test:workflow` all exit 0. `openspec validate --all --strict`: 13 passed.\n\n## Risk and scope\n\nThe changes stay in `controllers/tidbyt`, plus a workspace dependency on `@jimmie-potts/agent-state` in the lockfile, the development guide and OpenSpec. The shared controller v1 contract, agent-state and hub are unchanged. No device, account, hook, service or installation was touched. How long an unrefreshed installation persists is still unqualified; the 10 minute refresh bounds it.\n\nUI: the Tidbyt status frame is device UI outside `docs/work-guide/`, so it needs explicit human approval of this candidate before merge.\n\n## Remaining\n\nWiring to the running hub feed, installation and the visible check on the real display belong to #21. The issue stays open until merged-main CI is read back.\n\nRefs #19\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
